From 1122ec768f604e08fefcab470d2ed11e56539320 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mrinohk <5554998+Mrinohk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 23:24:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 18/31] cuda : persistent single-token layer-half kernels for
 Qwen3.5/3.6 MoE on sm_60

GGML_CUDA_P60_MEGA=1 (with GGML_CUDA_P60_MMVQ=1) runs each half of a gated-delta-net layer as one cooperative
launch at decode (one token, one sequence, no recurrent snapshots):
- GDN half: attn_norm, qkv (+ conv, silu, conv-state update), z, alpha, beta, recurrence (+ state update),
  gated norm, ssm_out, residual add. 3 phases.
- MoE half: post-attention norm, router top-8 + shared gate, expert gate/up + shared gate/up/down, expert down,
  weighted sum, residual add. 3 phases.
All blocks stay resident and sync with a software grid barrier between phases (counter grows across launches).
The matchers find a half by op and weight name from its RMS_NORM to its residual ADD and fall back to the
normal path on anything else (attention layers, snapshot state for MTP, other quant types, extra get_rows).
An ADD before such a norm is no longer fused into it. GGML_CUDA_P60_MEGA_DEBUG=1 logs why a match failed.

Not bit-exact: fp32 activations, no int8/fp16 activation rounding. 2x P100, 35B UD-Q4_K_XL, no speculation:
llama-bench tg128 85.6 -> 116.7 t/s; server 8-prompt bench 84.0 -> 113.6 t/s (greedy), 113.5 (prod sampler).
wikitext-2 ub=1 vs stock base: KLD 0.0044, PPL +0.25% +- 0.18%, same top 97.2% (production path: 0.0040,
97.8%). In a harness on real weights the MoE output error vs fp64 is ~1e-14 here vs ~1e-4 for int8 activations.
MTP decoding is unchanged (verify is multi-token).

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
